 :manifest/description
 "Canonical cross-repository trace equivalence manifest.
  Each entry binds a Clojure-generated CDRS trace to its Solidity
  fixture destination and records SHA-256 hashes for integrity verification.

  - :id             — unique logical identifier for this trace pair
  - :source         — path relative to Clojure repo root
  - :source-sha256  — SHA-256 of the source trace file (populated by sync)
  - :scenario       — optional .edn scenario file for regeneration
  - :destination    — path relative to :sew-repo-root
  - :cdrs-version   — trace format version (must be \"0.2\")
  - :review-scenario — identifier from EF_REVIEW_GUIDE.md if applicable
  - :purpose        — human-readable note
  - :solidity-test? — true if a Forge test method exists in
    TraceEquivalenceTest.sol replaying this trace.  A trace is NOT wired when
    it uses actions the basic vault harness cannot reproduce (yield-ops,
    evidence-module, slashing-module, register-stake/withdraw-stake side
    effects, successful escalation, or amounts below the contract's
    MIN_ESCROW_AMOUNT).  The actual wired set is derived from
    TraceEquivalenceTest.sol, not maintained here.

 :notes
 {:invariant-profile
  "solidity-equivalence-core-v1 (version 1).  See etc/solidity-invariant-profile.edn
   for the full mapping of Clojure invariants to Solidity check functions.
   7 invariants checked: conservation-of-funds, dispute-level-bounded,
   terminal-payout-exclusivity, held-reconstruction, state-transition-valid,
   escalation-monotonic, terminal-state-immutable."

  :stake-actions
  "register_stake and withdraw_stake are handled as no-ops in the Forge
   harness because stake is pre-established during setUp().  This is valid
   for traces that do not depend on stake state changing during replay.
   No stake lifecycle equivalence is asserted.  Traces requiring dynamic
   stake modification remain excluded."

  :pre-existing-fixtures
  "14 fixtures in test/foundry/traces/ are pre-existing and not part of the
   manifest-bound equivalence set.  They are reported as warnings by
   bb trace:solidity:verify and must not be counted toward the verified
   trace count.  Classification: legacy-golden-v0.1 (4), legacy-v2-baseline
   (3), negative-adversarial (7)."}

